            <titleStmt xml:id="titleStmt_cd6864b6">
               <title xml:id="title_545N200B2">Sketch and fair copy, autograph (Andante sostenuto)</title>
            </titleStmt>
            <pubStmt xml:id="pubStmt_5f482124"/>
            <physDesc xml:id="physDesc_7a6f8cf8">
               <extent xml:id="extent_9e8353d1">2 pages</extent>
               <dimensions unit="cm" xml:id="dimensions_6c1fabef">34,5 x 29</dimensions>
               <physMedium xml:id="physMedium_e2c493ae">1 folio. Written in ink on both pages (added pencil sketches at the bottom of one of the pages). Paper: 20 staves. Recto: "Andante sostenuto". End-dating: "15/9 53."</physMedium>
            </physDesc>
            <notesStmt xml:id="notesStmt_92507e90">
               <annot type="source_description" xml:id="annot_3e7753fd">
                  <p xml:id="idm87">A combination of this source and the fair copy of the sonata apparently comprises the earliest version with the following order of movements: Allegro grazioso, Allegretto Intermezzo, Andante sostenuto, Allegro commodo, including the bridge passage between the two last movements. As it may be seen from the datings the Andante was finished more than one year earlier than the first movement.</p>
               </annot>
            </notesStmt>
