         <manifestation label="" xml:id="source_d1e240">
            <titleStmt xml:id="titleStmt_cd099b8c">
               <title xml:id="title_545N201F3">Score, autograph, fair copy</title>
            </titleStmt>
            <physDesc xml:id="physDesc_9cd32f07">
               <extent xml:id="extent_cc89a81c">16 pages</extent>
               <dimensions unit="cm" xml:id="dimensions_fd3a98cd">34 x 26</dimensions>
               <physMedium xml:id="physMedium_e97b8db3">Four bifolios (the second torn apart in two pages), paginated 1-12, 13 (cancelled), 14-15 corrected in pencil to 20-21). Written in brown ink. Paper: 12 staves. Above the first stave on the first music page (p. 2): "Sonate". Contents: First movement and Andante sostenuto, con largezza. Later Hartmann moved the latter movement to "Klaverstykker fra ældre og nyere Tid", Opus 74 (HartW 120). Pencil additions on top of pp. 13 and 14 (=20) "Skrives ikke" (not to be copied), referring to the cancelled staves on the pages in question (equivalent with the last 36 bars of the first movement). This remark does not belong to the sonata but it was added when Hartmann later moved the gathering in question to the manuscript of Opus 74 (Andantino). At the bottom of p. 22 a remark is added, which also relates to the removal of this part of the manuscript to Opus 74: "<rend xml:id="idm134" rend="underline">NB</rend> Efter N<rend xml:id="idm135" rend="sup">o</rend> 3<rend xml:id="idm136" rend="sup">s</rend> Slutning <rend xml:id="idm137" rend="underline">tilbage</rend> til N<rend xml:id="idm138" rend="sup">o</rend> 4 pag. 19, Allegretto moderato" (After the end of No. 3 go <rend xml:id="idm139" rend="underline">back</rend> to No. 4 p. 19, Allegretto moderato).</physMedium>
            </physDesc>
